On Sunday 08 August 2004 20:22 5parrow (mail.gatech@gtg692n.edu) wrote:

> Raisse the Thaumaturge wrote:
> 
>> You can pick up a loadstone in a box (or a bag) without any trouble,
>> except that it's heavy, but if you have a "bare" loadstone in your
>> inventory it can't leave your person while it's cursed, meaning you
>> can't drop it, put it in a box or bag, throw it, or shoot it with a
>> sling.
> 
> Hmm. How about dipping it in a !oPoly?

That looked interesting enough to try in explore mode (instead of
telling you that you could use explore more yourself), and it turned
into a red gem and my movements were unencumbered.

It does break no-poly conduct, but if you don't care about that it's a
good way to get rid of it (if you happen not to have any holy water, or
scrolls of remove curse, etcetera).

Cancelling yourself with it in your inventory (take care to drop
everything you don't want cancelled if you do that; it won't cancel
*you*, but everything you're currently carrying) also uncurses the
loadstone so you can drop it.

